 filter bounds?', 'yes', 'current_code.py both dataset constructions in run_weight_eeg_raw and run_weight_x3d specify ll=0, rr=20.'),\n    ('Is the current final prediction solely from the double-head model?', 'yes', 'current_code.py final inference cell only executes run_weight_double_head and its append; X3D and raw EEG calls are commented out.'),\n    ('Are the declared weights_by_score used for the current blend?', 'no', 'current_code.py declares [0.24,0.28,0.24,0.24], but the weighted expression is commented out and np.mean is applied to the single active prediction.'),\n]\nreport = {\n    'observations': [{'observation': question, 'result': result, 'evidence': evidence} for question, result, evidence in observations],\n    'action_summary': 'Replace the sole v113 double-head prediction with an equal probability blend of the existing X3D and raw EEG families, averaging checkpoints and existing hemisphere views within each family. Historical improvements from adding these families motivate recovering ensemble diversity and excluding the sharply regressed double-head redesign; preserve trained architectures, strict checkpoint loading, filter bounds, and current time-reversal behavior. Reuse loaded models across hemisphere views, load checkpoint tensors on CPU, release models between checkpoints, and halve X3D loader batches to accommodate internal time-reversal TTA. Validate and normalize final probabilities, retain the required submission.csv schema and Kaggle paths, and replace notebook shell copies with Python equivalents. No training or inference was run; leaderboard improvement and checkpoint compatibility cannot be measured without the data and attached weights.'\n}\nPath('output/report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + '\\\\n')\ncompile(source, 'output/revised_code.py', 'exec')\nloaded = json.loads(Path('output/report.json').read_text())\nassert set(loaded) == {'observations', 'action_summary'}\nassert isinstance(loaded['action_summary'], str)\nassert all(set(item) == {'observation', 'result', 'evidence'} and item['result'] in {'yes', 'no'} for item in loaded['observations'])\nprint('Python syntax and report JSON validation passed.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
